  "authored_scope": "Random scenes use 12..30 per side, sampled independently; explicit random sizes may be 10..30. Sizes other than 18x18 and 28x28, and non-square grids, are synthetic extensions. The background is any non-red colour and is always the strict majority colour. Default scenes hold 2..6 mirror/shape pairs: line-only with probability 0.15, otherwise mixed point and line mirrors; explicit mirror_kinds may request point-only scenes. Shapes are random 8-connected blobs, and point-mirror shapes always have an off-axis cell. Line shapes may overhang the line end, sometimes touching it only diagonally. Shape and line extents grow moderately on grids with a minimum side of at least 22. Border clipping occurs occasionally, keeping at least half of each reflection in the grid. Optional occlusion lets reflections fall on other objects (about 20% of scenes by default); occlusion is permitted there, not forced. Explicit object scenes reconstruct the fixtures and are validated. Not supported: shapes touching two mirrors, multicoloured shapes, bent or diagonal mirrors, and colliding reflections of different colours.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Every shape is one 8-connected single-colour component that is 8-adjacent to exactly one red mirror and to no other shape.",
    "Distinct mirrors are never 8-adjacent, so each 4-connected red component is exactly one straight mirror and no diagonal red pattern appears.",
    "Point-mirror shapes in random scenes contain at least one cell off both axes through the red cell.",
    "The background colour is the strict majority of input cells, in both random and explicit scenes.",
    "Shape colours never equal red or the background.",
    "Reflections of different colours never share a cell.",
    "Every object paints at least one visible cell, and at least half of each in-grid reflection is visible; at least half of each reflection lies in the grid.",
    "Without occlusion, every footprint (mirror, shape and reflection) is separated from the others by at least one background cell.",
    "Retry loops are bounded (200 scene attempts x 150 placements per object); clearly infeasible counts are rejected up front."
  ],
  "semantic_review": {
    "status": "reviewed",
    "checks": [
      "Canonical fixtures exactly reconstructed;1000 independent seeds pass.",
      "1240 targeted scenes independently segmented into red4-components and shape8-components; all three reflection formulas and outputs match.",
      "Across800 defaults:1021 point,891 vertical and889 horizontal mirrors;53 clipped cells,48 occluded cells and22 diagonal-only line contacts.",
      "300 forced-occlusion six-object30x30 scenes include115 occluded reflected cells and28 clipped cells; occupied input cells are preserved.",
      "80 all-kind30x30 scenes and60 wide30x12 scenes pass.",
      "30 adversarial trials pass, including the previously mismatching3x3 low-background scene now rejected.",
      "1000 independent seeds 20000..20999; approved validation fixtures reconstructed exactly; canonical replay reported separately"
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Random input side10..30 (sampled12..30),1..8 mirrors, object sizes limited by procedural blob templates and grid-dependent caps.",
      "Random fixed counts require40 cells of canvas per object: a conservative sampler-density restriction, not a mathematical infeasibility theorem.",
      "Different-colour reflection collisions and touching mirrors are rejected; at least one cell must be painted. Random objects retain at least half their in-grid reflected cells visible."
    ]
  },
